From 898a4ac3dfde05421f9db6af0074f2ba8829e9b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matthew <matthewhale@live.com.au>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 16:42:46 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 12/59] render.xvt_cockpit: X-Wing vs TIE Fighter cockpits and
 cockpit-off HUD

1998 flight draws XvT's cockpit art (Balance of Power CP640 <craft>.int and
view LFDs, copied into resources/xvt_cockpit by the packaging script) for the
X-Wing, Y-Wing, A-Wing and B-Wing, in every cockpit view including the
cockpit-off HUD (X12HUD and so on).

- X-Wing's instruments keep their own state and sprites and move to where
  XvT's layout has the same role (laser charge/ready, warheads, shields,
  hull, power, s-foils, gunsight marks), paired left to right within each
  role. Other elements and panes move with their nearest mapped element.
  X-Wing's large damage overlays are not drawn.
- The XvT-style CMD fills XvT's CMD screen (no backdrop), with speed and
  throttle on its bottom row; the throttle bar and speed pane are hidden.
  The clock and max speed go to XvT's speed/throttle readout boxes.
- Messages move from the 1998 bottom strip to under the radars, without
  the strip background.
- Cockpit off: the forward panel keeps updating; shields wrap XvT's HUD
  hull icon, power bars go to the screen edges, warheads and clock to the
  lower right boxes. The widescreen HUD splits the art at x 182/456 so the
  CMD block stays whole.
- Video settings toggle "XvT Cockpit and HUD" (needs the XvT targeting
  computer).
